# Professional English only

- **Always use professional, plain English in chat, plans, GO lists, and commit messages.**
- **Never use slang, dialect parody, broken shorthand, or “street” tone.**
- **Never use racial slurs or demeaning language in the agent’s voice.**
- Prefer short, precise sentences. Define terms instead of inventing jargon (for example, say “still-active order statuses” — not “open-ish”).
- When explaining systems, name the exact statuses, APIs, or files involved.
